menu "LCD I2C Configuration"

    config LCD_I2C_SDA_GPIO
        int "I2C data GPIO (HW-221 A1 -> module SDA)"
        range 0 SOC_GPIO_OUT_RANGE_MAX
        default 25
        help
            I2C SDA to the PCF8574 backpack through the HW-221 (TXS0108E) level
            shifter. Default 25, verified on hardware: free next to the robotic arm
            (1/3 PC link, UART0; 14/27 console, UART1; 16/17 servo bus, UART2) and the
            TFT (5, 18, 21, 22, 23), and not a strapping pin. Internal pull-ups stay
            disabled.

    config LCD_I2C_SCL_GPIO
        int "I2C clock GPIO (HW-221 A2 -> module SCL)"
        range 0 SOC_GPIO_OUT_RANGE_MAX
        default 26
        help
            I2C SCL, 100 kHz (PCF8574 maximum). Default 26, chosen for the same
            reasons as SDA. Internal pull-ups stay disabled.

    config LCD_I2C_ADDR
        hex "PCF8574 I2C address (7 bits)"
        range 0x08 0x77
        default 0x27
        help
            0x27 is a PCF8574 with A0-A2 open (verified on the module); a PCF8574A
            answers in 0x38..0x3F. If this address does not answer, lcd_init() scans
            the bus, logs every address found and, if exactly one device answers,
            uses it with a warning (lcd_get_info() reports the address in use).

endmenu
